{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"CI builds ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"text":" on every push and sums the resulting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"text":" sizes for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"text":" each store their running ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" in a private ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"text":" property, read by ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":". Every one of those ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":"s captures ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In practice, a completed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"text":" operation: without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","isActive":true},{"text":" for the rest of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":" safety net this guarantee supports.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","isActive":true},{"text":" only ever go active once ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" have confirmed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":" is already ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" — both fall back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"text":" can never be observed alongside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A parent view that reads ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"text":" (via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"text":" in the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" — the pattern ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" property read in a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":". This guarantee is about ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" case could be affected.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Performance"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/load(_:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"type":"text","text":", showing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" while it’s in flight and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapping its outcome to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"load(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/load(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"load","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateSto